        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10b511b747f34d5287ee765f2da11855",
      "statement": "The stub-vs-real lane switch happens in `buildRouteTable()` in src/index.ts: when `hasSupabaseEnv()` returns true (SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY both present), routes are wired through `createSupabaseSource()` real PostgREST readers; otherwise, clearly-marked stub doubles from `./stubs.ts` serve every route.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/dashboard-api/src/index.ts#L164-L186",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a31962309b968d7aea08dff26967cb73780b726c6c9dc77de3710e6a9c57383e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/dashboard-api/src/supabase.ts#L44-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6d31aeb33eeb30638c447f861517e4f4b8ef5f2e15098bd8e96bd0b0aff2a478:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dbd85f2409084c7f8f1af2fb2473fb39",
      "statement": "Every real-lane route handler is wrapped with `failClosed()`, which catches `UpstreamError` thrown by `supaGet()` on any non-OK PostgREST response and maps it to the contract §2 `upstream_empty` (502) error envelope with `upstream_status` in details. The worker never silently falls back to stubs when the service-role key is present.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/dashboard-api/src/index.ts#L150-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4851d8cb020bf87f8778d35121b4b8c1ad50a2855a67aef61cbbbc33a9fb5311:"
